    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d187">

                <pb facs="0299" n="219" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg219"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Mutual Guarantee (Locarno)/394:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Daniels</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-03-09T23:00:00-06:00">March 9, 1936—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 10—11:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I venture to express the hope that opportunity may offer for the President to
                    tender good offices to avert war in Europe. If we had acted promptly in August,
                    1914, that catastrophe might have been averted or its tragedy ended earlier.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Daniels</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
